2 CONT * Born -	22 May 1813, Palermo
2 CONT * Died -	4 December 1860 (aged 47), Pisa
2 CONT * Burial -	Basilica of Santa Chiara, Naples
2 CONT * Prince Leopoldo Beniamino Giuseppe of Bourbon-Two Sicilies, Count of Syracuse (22 May 1813, Palermo – 4 December 1860, Pisa) was a member of the House of Bourbon-Two Sicilies.
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT * Leopold was the fifth son of Francis I of the Two Sicilies and his second wife Maria Isabella of Spain.[1] Leopold's elder brother, Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies, considered a marriage between Leopold and Princess Marie of Or
2 CONC léans, but the negotiations with her father, Louis-Philippe of France, foundered over the French uprisings in 1834 and Louis-Philippe's refusal to grant Marie her part of the "donation-partage" of his lands (a condition Ferdinand 
2 CONC had put in place for the marriage to occur).
2 CONT ===Marriage and issue===
2 CONT * Leopold ultimately married Princess Maria of Savoy-Carignan, second-eldest daughter of Prince Joseph Maria of Savoy-Carignan, Count of Villafranca and his wife Pauline Benedictine de Quélen de Vauguyon, on 16 June 1837[1] in Nap
2 CONC les. Leopold and Maria had only one child, Isabella, who died less than a year after her birth in 1838. [edit] Titles, styles, honours and arms
2 CONT ===Titles and styles===
2 CONT * 22 May 1813 – 4 December 1860: His Royal Highness The Count of Syracuse
2 CONT ===Honours===
2 CONT * Knight of the Orders of the King of France (1826)
2 CONT * Knight of the Order of Saint Januarius (1813)
2 CONT * '''Knight of the Spanish Order of the Golden Fleece (1813)'''
2 CONT * Knight Grand Cross of the Order of Saint Ferdinand and of Merit
2 CONT * Knight Grand Cross with Collar of the Order of Charles III
2 CONT * Knight of the Order of the Black Eagle
2 CONT * Knight of the Order of the Most Holy Annunciation
