2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p11448.htm#i114471 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/I/per_page.php?id=5942 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GScid=639283&GRid=7032093& Find a Grave]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umberto_I_of_Italy Wikipedia]
2 CONT *'''King of Italy:''' Reign 9 January 1878 – 29 July 1900 (22 years, 201 days)
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Victor-Emmanuel-II-of-Italy/1354718 Victor Emmanuel II] '''Successor:'''	[http://www.geni.com/people/Victor-Emmanuel-III-of-Italy/376469227150012924 Victor Emmanuel III]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Umberto I (14. maaliskuuta 1844 – 29. heinäkuuta 1900) (Umberto Rainerio Carlo Emanuele Giovanni Maria Ferdinando Eugenio, Principe del Piemonte) oli Italian kuningas 9. tammikuuta 1878 lähtien kuolemaansa saakka. Vasemmistossa hä
2 CONC n oli vihattu vanhoillisuutensa vuoksi ja lopulta anarkisti Gaetano Bresci murhasi hänet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Umberto oli Sardinian kuningas Viktor Emanuel II:n (vuodesta 1861 Italian kuningas) ja arkkiherttuatar Adelaiden poika. Hän syntyi Torinossa, joka oli tuolloin Sardinian kuningaskunnan pääkaupunki. Maaliskuussa 1858 hän liittyi Sa
2 CONC rdinian armeijaan ja taisteli Solferinossa 1859 ja Custozassa 1866.
2 CONT
2 CONT 21. huhtikuuta 1868 Umberto nai serkkunsa, Savoijin prinsessa Margherita Teresa Giovannan. Heidän poikansa olivat Viktor Emanuel, Napolin prinssi ja Viktor Emanuel, Italian kuningas.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/L29X-FSL
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umberto_I_of_Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT Umberto I or Humbert I (Italian: Umberto Ranieri Carlo Emanuele Giovanni Maria Ferdinando Eugenio di Savoia, English: Humbert Ranier Charles Emmanuel John Mary Ferdinand Eugene of Savoy; 14 March 1844 – 29 July 1900), nicknamed th
2 CONC e Good (in Italian il Buono), was the King of Italy from 9 January 1878 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Umberto's reign saw Italy attempt colonial expansion into the Horn of Africa, successfully gaining Eritrea and Somalia despite being defeated by Abyssinia at the Battle of Adowa in 1896. In 1882, he approved the Triple Alliance wi
2 CONC th the German Empire and Austria-Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was deeply loathed in leftist circles because of his conservatism and support of the Bava-Beccaris massacre in Milan. He was especially hated by anarchists, who attempted an assassination on him during the first year of his rei
2 CONC gn. He was killed by another anarchist, Gaetano Bresci, two years after the Bava-Beccaris massacre.
