2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p11069.htm#i110684 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[https://geneall.net/de/name/6078/maria-josepha-infantin-von-portugal/ Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00007694&tree=LEO Genealogics]
2 CONT *[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infanta_Maria_Josepha_of_Portugal Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Maria José of Portugal (or of Beja or Braganza; full name Maria José Joana Eulália Leopoldina Adelaide Isabel Carolina Micaela Rafaela Gabriela Francisca de Assis e de Paula Inês Sofia Joaquina Teresa Benedita Bernardina o
2 CONC f Braganza; March 19, 1857 – Munich, March 11, 1943), sometimes known in English as Maria Josepha, was a Portuguese infanta, later Duchess in Bavaria by marriage. She was the maternal grandmother of King Leopold III of Belgium.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Life
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria José was the fourth child and third daughter of King Miguel I of Portugal and his wife Adelaide of Löwenstein-Wertheim-Rosenberg. Among her sisters were Maria Ana, Grand Duchess of Luxemburg and Maria Antónia, Duchess of Par
2 CONC ma. Her only brother was Miguel II, Duke of Braganza.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married on April 29, 1874 Karl-Theodor, Duke in Bavaria, the younger brother of Elisabeth of Bavaria, better known as "Sissi".
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple lived in München, where they founded the Herzog Carl Theodor Eye Clinic, that still exists today.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria José died in 1943 at the age of 85, and is buried in Tegernsee Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie Adelheid (1875-1957)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth Gabriele Valérie Marie (1876-1965), future Queen Elisabeth of Belgium, married Albert I of Belgium.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Gabrielle (1878-1912), married Rupprecht, Crown Prince of Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludwig Wilhelm (1884-1968)
2 CONT
2 CONT Franz Joseph (1888-1912)
