2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Princess Antonietta of the Two Sicilies
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Antonia Josepha (Antonietta) (Naples, March 16, 1851 – Freiburg im Breisgau, September 12, 1938), was a Princess of the Two Sicilies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Antonia was the eldest daughter of Francesco Count of Trapani (son of Francis I of the Two Sicilies) and Princess Isabella of Tuscany (daughter of Leopold II, Grand Duke of Tuscany).
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Antonia married on June 8, 1868 in Rome with Prince Alfonso of Bourbon-Sicily, son of King Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had twelve children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Ferdinando Pius, Duke of Calabria (1869-1960), married Princess Maria Ludwiga Theresia of Bavaria, a daughter of King Ludwig III of Bavaria. This marriage had six issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Carlos Tancredi (1870-1949), married in 1901 to Princess Maria de las Mercedes of Spain. Had Issue. Re-married in 1907 to Princess Louise of Orléans of France. Grandparents of King Juan Carlos I of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Francesco di Paola (1873-1876)
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Immacolata (1874-1947), married in 1906, to Prince Johann Georg of Saxony, a younger son of Infanta Maria Ana of Portugal and King George of Saxony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Cristina (1877-1947), married in 1900, to Archduke Peter Ferdinand of Austria-Tuscany, a younger son of Ferdinand IV, Grand Duke of Tuscany and his heir as head of the Grand Ducal house of Tuscany.
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria di Grazia (1878-1973), married in 1908, to Prince Dom Luiz of Orléans and Bragança.
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Giuseppina Antonietta (1880-1971)
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Gennaro (1882-1944), married in 1922, to Beatrice Bordessa, Countess of Villa Colli. Her title was by grant of the Count of Caserta,1923
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Ranieri, Duke of Castro (1883-1973), married in 1923 to his cousin, Countess Marie Caroline Zamoyska, a daughter of Count Andrzej Zamoyski.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Filippo (1885-1949), married to Marie Louise of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Francesco d'Assisi (1888-1914)
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Gabriele (1897-1975), married in 1927 to Princess Malgorzata Czartoryska and in 1932 to Cecilia Lubomirska, daughter of Prince Kasimir Lubomirski.
2 CONT
2 CONT PVD's 25th cousin five times removed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Carolina Bourbon-Two-Sicilies is an interesting addition to the consanguinity discussion - as her mother's parents were double first cousins and her mother married her uncle. She is listed with a consanguinity index of 22.98
2 CONC % http://thepeerage.com/p11237.htm#i112363
