1 NAME Aymon-Jean-Baptiste-Marie /de Faucigny-Lucinge/
2 GIVN Aymon-Jean-Baptiste-Marie
2 _MARNM de Faucigny-Lucinge
1 NAME Prince Aymon de Faucigny-Lucinge et Coligny
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 MAY 1862
2 ADDR
3 CITY Paris
3 STAE Île-de-France
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 AUG 1922
2 PLAC Chateau de Charddonneux
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 TITL Prince
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Prince" Aymon-Jean-Baptiste-Marie de Faucigny-Lucinge was one of the last French princes. He was born in 1862 to Louis Charles Rodolphe de Faucigny-Lucinge and Amanda de Mailly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aymon's title of "Prince" was semi-official as he was from an aristocratic family in Savoy which had ties to the old royalty and was used as a rank.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aymon Jean-Baptiste Marie de Faucigny-Lucinge et Coligny est né le 30 mai 1862, 17 rue de la Madeleine à Paris (8ème arrondissement). Il est le fils de Louis Charles Rodolphe de Faucigny-Lucinge et Coligny, prince de Lucinge et Cy
2 CONC stria et du Saint-Empire Romain, et de Henriette Victorine Marie Amanda de Mailly, 29 ans[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Il a épousé Carolyn Foster, veuve Stickney, le 2 juillet 1913 à Londres
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.thepeerage.com/p8693.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Acte de naissance: Acte #724, Naissances 1862 Paris VIIIème, Archives de Paris en ligne cote V4E 881 (vue 12), consulté le 12 décembre 2017 ↑ "England and Wales Marriage Registration Index, 1837-2005," database, FamilySearch (http
2 CONC s://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:26Z9-33P : 22 May 2014), Carolyn Foster Stickney and null, 1913; from “England & Wales Marriages, 1837-2005,” database, findmypast (http://www.findmypast.com : 2012); citing 1913, quarter 3, vol
2 CONC . 1A, p. 1225, St. George Hanover Square, London, England, General Register Office, Southport, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served with distinction in the United States army in World War I and achieved the Medal of Honor from the President and the rank of Captain:
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://valor.militarytimes.com/recipient.php?recipientid=18548
2 CONT
2 CONT Pictures of his medals: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gmic.co.uk/topic/70376-capitaine-aymon-de-faucigny-lucinge-et-coligny/
