1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marie Letitia Eugenie Catherine Adelaide Bonaparte
2 CONT * Princesse Napoléon 
2 CONT * Birth: 20 Dec 1866 	Palais Royal 
2 CONT * Death: 25 Oct 1926 	Château de Moncalieri  (aged 59)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT * Father: Napoléon Joseph Charles Paul Bonaparte (9 September 1822 – 17 March 1891)
2 CONT * Mother: Princess Maria Clotilde of Savoy (2 March 1843 – 25 June 1911) 
2 CONT * Spouse: Prince Amadeo, Duke of Aosta (30 May 1845 – 18 January 1890) - married on 11 September 1888 at the Royal Palace of Turin in Turin, Italy (aged 22).
2 CONT * Issue: Prince Umberto, Count of Salemi  (22 June 1889 – 19 October 1918) (died of the Spanish flu during World War I)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Titles
2 CONT
2 CONT * November 20, 1866 - September 11, 1888: Her Imperial Highness Princess Marie-Laetitia Bonaparte;
2 CONT * September 11, 1888 - January 18, 1890: Her Imperial and Royal Highness the Duchess of Aosta;
2 CONT * January 18, 1890 - October 25, 1926: Her Imperial and Royal Highness the Dowager Duchess of Aosta.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Widow Marie-Laetitia had a relationship that caused a scandal with Norbert Fischer, a young soldier twenty years younger. Upon her death on October 25, 1926, it was discovered that Fisher had become, following the death of Prince 
2 CONC Humbert, the sole heir of the Dowager Duchess of Aosta. In 1928, he married the singer Vina Bovy.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
