1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Princess Louise of Orléans
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia;
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Louise_d%27Orl%C3%A9ans_%281882%E2%80%931958%29
2 CONT
2 CONT "Louise of Orléans, (Cannes, 1882 - Seville, 1958) was a Princess of the Two-Sicilies and maternal grandmother of King Juan Carlos I of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the youngest daughter of Philippe of Orléans (1838-1894), Count of Paris and claimant to the French throne as "Philippe VII". Her mother was Princess Marie Isabelle of Orléans (1848-1919), infanta of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 16, 1907, she married in Wood Norton, England Prince Carlos of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (1870-1949), prince of the Two-Sicilies and widower of Mercedes, Princess of Asturias, infanta of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple lived in Madrid and had 4 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Carlo of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (1908-1936). Killed in the Spanish Civil War fighting on the Nationalist side.
2 CONT
2 CONT Doña Maria de los Dolores of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (1909-1996). In 1937, she married Jozef Prince Czartoryski (1907-1946) and had one surviving son, Adam. She remarried to Carlos Chias on 1950.
2 CONT
2 CONT Doña Maria Mercedes of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (1910-2000) who married Infante Juan, Count of Barcelona and became the mother of current reining King Juan Carlos I of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria de la Esperanza of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (1914-2005), who married Prince Pedro Gastão of Orléans-Braganza.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1931, when the Spanish Republic was proclaimed, the family left Spain for Italy and later Switzerland. In 1939, after the victory of Franco in the Spanish civil War they returned to Spain and settled in Seville."
