1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Ferdinand_Pius,_Duke_of_Calabria '''en.wikipedia.org....''']; 
2 CONT * Prince Ferdinand Pius (Ferdinando Pio Maria), Duke of Calabria (25 July 1869, Rome – 7 January 1960, Lindau), was head of the House of Bourbon-Two Sicilies and pretender to the throne of the extinct Kingdom of the Two Sicilies f
2 CONC rom 1934 to 1960.
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT * Ferdinand was the eldest child and son of Prince Alfonso, Count of Caserta and his wife Princess Maria Antonietta of Bourbon-Two Sicilies. He was a grandson of Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies and an elder brother of Prince Carl
2 CONC os of Bourbon-Two Sicilies, Maria Immaculata, Princess Johann Georg of Saxony, Maria Cristina, Archduchess Peter Ferdinand of Austria, Maria di Grazia, Princess Imperial of Brazil, Prince Ranieri, Duke of Castro, Prince Philip of 
2 CONC Bourbon-Two Sicilies, and Prince Gabriel of Bourbon-Two Sicilies.
