1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Full name
2 CONT
2 CONT Portuguese: Maria da Graça Pia Clara Ana Teresa Isabela Adelaide Apolônia Ágata Cecília Filomena Antônia Lúcia Cristina Catarina
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Maria_di_Grazia_of_Bourbon-Two_Sicilies
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Dona Maria delle Grazie Pia Chiara Anna Teresa Isabella Liutgarda Apollonia Ágata Cecillia Filomena Antonia Lucia Cristina Catarina di Borbone e Borbone, Princesa Real das Duas Sicílias, Princesa de Bourbon(-Anjou).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Princess Maria di Grazia (Full Italian name: Maria delle Grazie Pia Chiara Anna Teresa Isabella Luitgarda Apollonia Agata Cecilia Filomena Antonia Lucia Cristina Caterina di Borbone (12 August 1878, Cannes, France – 20 June 1973, 
2 CONC Mandelieu-la-Napoule, France was a princess of Bourbon-Two Sicilies and princess of Orléans-Braganza through her marriage to Prince Luiz of Orléans-Braganza.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria was the daughter of Prince Alfonso of Bourbon-Two Sicilies, Count of Caserta and his wife Princess Antonietta of Bourbon-Two Sicilies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria married Prince Luiz Maria of Orléans-Braganza, son of Prince Gaston of Orléans, Count of Eu and his wife Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil, on 4 November 1908 in Cannes, France.
2 CONT  Maria and Luiz had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Pedro Henrique Afonso Felipe Maria Miguel Gabriel Rafael Gonzaga of Orléans-Braganza (13 September 1909 - 5 July 1981) married Princess Maria Elisabeth of Bavaria (1914 - 2011) at Nymphenburg Palace on 19 August 1937. Pedro
2 CONC  Henrique and Maria had twelve children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Luiz Gastão Antônio Maria Filipe Miguel Gabriel Rafael Gonzaga of Orléans-Braganza (19 February 1911 - 8 September 1931)
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Pia Maria Raniera Isabella Antonia Vitoria Thereza Amélia Gerarda Raimunda Anna Micaela Rafaela Gabriela Gonzaga of Orléans-Braganza (4 March 1913 - 24 October 2000) married René, Count of Nicolay at Paris on 12 August 19
2 CONC 33. Pia Maria and René had three sons.
