1 OCCU Prince Imperial of Brazil
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dom Luiz Maria Philippe Pedro de Alcantara Gastão Miguel Gabriel Raphael Gonzaga de Orleans e Bragança, Príncipe do Brasil, Príncipe de Orleans e Bragança, Príncipe Imperial do Brasil (1908-1920). /// Sepultamento:
2 CONC  na chapelle royale Saint-Louis de Dreux.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Prince Luís of Orléans-Braganza (26 January 1878 – 26 March 1920), was an heir to the throne of the Empire of Brazil. He was born in Brazil, the second son of Prince Gaston, Count of Eu, and Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was exiled along with his family as the result of the 1889 coup d'état that resulted in the formation of the republic. In 1908, the year he was married, his older brother Pedro resigned his claim to the imperial throne leaving 
2 CONC Luís heir apparent. In this role he worked with monarchists in Brazil in several attempts to restore the monarchy. At the outbreak of World War I he enlisted as an officer with the British Armed Forces and saw action in Flanders w
2 CONC here he contracted a virulent form of rheumatism that caused his death at the age of 42. His efforts on behalf of the Allies of World War I saw him decorated by Belgium, France and Great Britain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Luís was born at Petrópolis on 26 January 1878, to Prince Gaston d'Orléans, Count of Eu, and Isabel, Princess Imperial of Brazil. His paternal grandparents were Prince Louis, Duke of Nemours, and Princess Victoria of Saxe-Coburg a
2 CONC nd Gotha, while his maternal grandparents were Pedro II, Emperor of Brazil, and Princess Teresa Cristina of the Two Sicilies. He was named after his paternal grandfather. His name in full was Luís Maria Filipe Pedro de Alcântara G
2 CONC astão Miguel Rafael Gonzaga. As the second oldest son of the heiress to the imperial throne of Brazil, he was not expected to one day ascend to the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Lu%C3%ADs_of_Orl%C3%A9ans-Braganza_(1878%E2%80%931920)
