2 CONT
2 CONT "Prince Michel of Bourbon-Parma (born Michel Marie Xavier Waldemar Georg Robert Karl Eymar; 4 March 1926 – 7 July 2018)[1] was a French businessman, soldier and racing car driver, who was a member of deposed sovereign ducal House 
2 CONC of Bourbon-Parma.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a son of Prince René of Bourbon-Parma (1894–1962) and his wife Princess Margaret of Denmark (1895–1992). Paternally, he was a grandson of Robert I, Duke of Parma (1848–1907), while through his mother he was a great-grandson
2 CONC  of King Christian IX of Denmark (1818–1906). Prince Michel was also the younger brother of Queen Anne of Romania (1923–2016)."
2 CONT
