1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Anna_of_Saxony_(1903%E2%80%931976)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p11194.htm#i111931
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Anna of Saxony (1903–1976)
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Anna Monika Pia of Saxony, Duchess of Saxony (Full German name: Prinzessin Anna Monika Pia von Sachsen, Herzogin zu Sachsen[1][2]) (born 4 May 1903 in Lindau, Bavaria[1][2]; died 8 February 1976 in Munich, Bavaria, German
2 CONC y[1][2]) was the seventh and youngest child of Frederick Augustus III of Saxony and his wife Archduchess Luise of Austria, Princess of Tuscany and a younger sister of Georg, Crown Prince of Saxony and Friedrich Christian, Margrave
2 CONC  of Meissen.[1][2] Through her marriage to Archduke Joseph Francis of Austria, Anna was a member an Archduchess and Princess of Austria and Princess of Hungary, Croatia, and Bohemia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT While pregnant with Anna, her mother Luise left Saxony on 9 December 1902 without her children. Anna was born during her parent's separation and after her birth, Luise sent the infant to the royal court in Dresden where she was ra
2 CONC ised with her five siblings by her father Frederick Augustus. It was erroneously believed that Anna was the daughter of André Giron, her siblings' French tutor with whom her mother briefly lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna married Archduke Joseph Francis of Austria, eldest son of Archduke Joseph August of Austria and his wife Princess Auguste Maria of Bavaria, on 4 October 1926 at Schloss Sibyllenort in Sibyllenort, Silesia, Germany.[1][2] Anna
2 CONC  and Joseph Francis had eight children:[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Margarethe of Austria (born 17 August 1925; died 3 May 1979) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Ilona of Austria (born 20 April 1927) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Anna-Theresia Gabriella of Austria (born 19 April 1928; died 28 November 1984) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduke Joseph Arpád of Austria (born 8 February 1933) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduke István Dominik Anton Umberto of Austria (born 1 July 1934) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Maria Kynga Beatrix of Austria (born 27 August 1938) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduke Géza Ladislaus of Austria (born 14 November 1940) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduke Michael Koloman of Austria (born 5 May 1942) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifteen years after the death of Joseph Francis in Carcavelos, Portugal on 25 September 1957, Anna married Reginald Kazanjian (1905-1990) in a civil ceremony on 28 July 1972 in Geneva, Switzerland, and in a religious ceremony on 9
2 CONC  September 1972 in Veyrier, Switzerland.[1][2]
