1 OCCU Archduke of Austria; Grand Duke of Tuscany (Nov. 8, 1948 - Jan. 21, 1984), Archduke of Austria; Head of the House of Habsburg-Tuscany (Nov. 8
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archduke_Gottfried_of_Austria en.wikipedia...] ; 
2 CONT * Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT ===Full name===
2 CONT * German: Gottfried Maria Joseph Peter Ferdinand Hubert Anton Rupert Leopold Heinrich Ignaz Alfons
2 CONT * House 	House of Habsburg-Lorraine
2 CONT * Father 	Archduke Peter Ferdinand of Austria
2 CONT * Mother 	Princess Maria Cristina of Bourbon-Two Sicilies
2 CONT * Born 	14 March 1902
2 CONT
2 CONT * Archduke Gottfried of Austria (German: Gottfried Maria Joseph Peter Ferdinand Hubert Anton Rupert Leopold Heinrich Ignaz Alfons, Erzherzog von Österreich, Prinz von Toskana[1][2]) (14 March 1902, Linz, Upper Austria, Austria–Hun
2 CONC gary[1][2] – 21 January 1984, Bad Ischl, Upper Austria, Austria[1][2]) was a member of the Tuscan line of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine and Archduke and Prince of Austria, Prince of Hungary, Bohemia, and Tuscany by birth. Gottfri
2 CONC ed was the titular Grand Duke of Tuscany from 8 November 1948 to 21 January 1984.
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT * Gottfried was the eldest child and son[1][2] of Archduke Peter Ferdinand of Austria and his wife Princess Maria Cristina of Bourbon-Two Sicilies.[1][2] Gottfried was raised with his three siblings in Salzburg and Vienna until th
2 CONC e end of World War I in 1918 when his family emigrated and moved to Lucerne, Switzerland.
2 CONT ===Marriage and issue===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gottfried '''married''' Princess Dorothea of Bavaria, fifth child and fourth daughter of Prince Franz of Bavaria and his wife Princess Isabella Antonie of Croÿ, on 2 August 1938 civilly and religiously on 3 August 1938 in Sárvár
2 CONC , Kingdom of Hungary.[1][2] Gottfried and Dorothea had four children together:[1][2]
2 CONT * Archduchess Elisabeth of Austria, Princess of Tuscany (born 2 October 1939)
2 CONT * Archduchess Alice of Austria, Princess of Tuscany (born 29 April 1941)
2 CONT * Archduke Leopold Franz of Austria, Prince of Tuscany (born 25 October 1942)
2 CONT * Archduchess Maria Antoinette of Austria, Princess of Tuscany (born 16 September 1950)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Titles and styles===
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 March 1902 – 8 November 1948: His Imperial and Royal Highness Archduke and Prince Gottfried of Austria; Prince Gottfried of Hungary, Bohemia, and Tuscany 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 November 1948 - 21 January 1984: His Imperial and Royal Highness The Grand Duke of Tuscany
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Honours===
2 CONT * Knight of the Austrian Order of the Golden Fleece - Austrian branch
