1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.schoolofwisdom.com/news/wilhelmine-keyserling-1921---2010-passes-on/ Willy Keyserling died peacefully in her sleep on October 4, 2010. She is survived by thousands of friends and students in Vienna and a
2 CONC ll over the world. "Willy was a one of a kind, a true spiritual revolutionary. And a Princess, truly, on all levels. She taught us by her life how to be a real person, an individual expression of God." Ralph
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelmine Keyserling was an exemplary woman for the new age of sexual equality. She developed herself as an autonomous individual, and yet maintained her femininity, living with her husband as a friend and equal partner for over 
2 CONC fifty years. She was both housewife and Earth Priestess, partner and innovator. She nurtured and supported her husband, Arnold Keyserling, in countless ways, yet she did not neglect her own soul, her own work. With Arnold's help a
2 CONC nd encouragement she developed her own understanding, fulfilled her own potentials. She was able to find and travel her own path, parallel to that of her husband, not behind it. Her Yin energies and perspective balance and complem
2 CONC ent the energies and insights of her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arnold and Willy supported each other, and worked with each other, and yet each had their own fields of expertise, their own places and times to shine. Their way as husband and wife followed the Tao Te symbol. The work of each con
2 CONC tained a piece of the other, and both depended upon, supported and complemented the other, and yet they were very different and separate and distinct - balanced and equal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1962 Arnold Keyserling moved from India to Vienna, Austria, to work on building the Wheel - a thinking tool developed by Arnold and his wife Wilhelmine - and on bringing the culture and knowledge of the East, particularly that 
2 CONC of India, to Western Europe. Arnold and his wife Wilhelmine were instrumental in starting the Yoga movement in Europe in the early sixties. Then in the seventies and eighties, the Keyserling's focus changed again as they became le
2 CONC aders of the Human Potential movement in Western and Central Europe. Arnold Keyserling was elected President of the European Humanistic Psychology Association. Arnold and Wilhelmine Keyserling also became one of the first groups t
2 CONC o introduce Native American shamans and shamanism to Europe in the 1980's.
