2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_Joseph_II,_Prince_of_Liechtenstein '''Wikipedia.....''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Franz Joseph II, Prince of Liechtenstein, (Franz Joseph Maria Aloys Alfred Karl Johannes Heinrich Michael Georg Ignaz Benediktus Gerhardus Majella), was the Sovereign Prince of Liechtenstein  from 1938 until his death. His full ti
2 CONC tle was Fürst von und zu Liechtenstein, Herzog von Troppau und Jägerndorf, Graf zu Rietberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT
2 CONT *Prince of Liechtenstein reign 1938–1989
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [Franz  I] '''Successor:''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Hans-Adam-II/6000000003365888478 Hans-Adam II]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.britannica.com/biography/Francis-Joseph-II
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/15590898/franz_josef_maria_aloys_alfred_karl_johannes_heinrich_mi-von_liechtenstein
2 CONT
2 CONT Sovereign Prince of Liechtenstein. He was born the son of Prince Alois von Liechtenstein and Archduchess Elisabeth Amelia of Austria. His Godfather was Kaiser Franz Josef I of Austria-Hungary. Prince Franz Josef II married Countes
2 CONC s Gina von Wilczek. He was the father of reigning Prince Hans-Adam. He became Sovereign Prince of Liechtenstein in 1938. He is well remembered for keeping his country out of the second world war and saving many people from certain
2 CONC  death. In 1984 he handed over most of his day-to-day responsibilities to his son Prince Hans-Adam while retaining the title of Sovereign Prince. He was widely mourned on his death and is fondly remembered by the people of Liechte
2 CONC nstein.
