1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Golden Fleece - Knights: Austrian Branch===
2 CONT * [http://thepeerage.com/p11180.htm#i111800 '''the peerage....''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodor Salvator Erzherzog von Österreich1 M, #111800, b. 9 October 1899, d. 8 April 1978
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodor Salvator Erzherzog von Österreich was born on 9 October 1899 at [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Datei:Wallsee_Schloss_2.jpg '''Wallsee Castle''']. He was the son of Franz Salvator Erzherzog von Österreich and Marie Valerie E
2 CONC rzherzogin von Österreich.1 He married Maria Theresa Gräfin von Waldburg zu Zeil und Trauchburg, daughter of Georg Fürst von Waldburg zu Zeil und Trauchburg and Marie Therese Altgräfin zu Salm-Reifferscheidt-Raitz, on 28 July 1926
2 CONC  at Zeil Castle.2 He died on 8 April 1978 at age 78 at Amstetten, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the title of Erzherzog von Österreich.1 He was given the name of Theodore Salvator Petrus Realinus Maria Josef Ignatius von Habsburg-Lothringen at birth. Children of Theodor Salvator Erzherzog von Österreich and Maria Th
2 CONC eresa Gräfin von Waldburg zu Zeil und Trauchburg
2 CONT
2 CONT # Franz Salvator Erzherzog von Österreich b. 10 Sep 1927
2 CONT #Theresia Monika Erzherzogin von Österreich b. 9 Jan 1931
2 CONT # Maria Immaculata Erzherzogin von Österreich b. 7 Dec 1933
2 CONT # Karl Salvator Erzherzog von Österreich b. 23 Jun 1936
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Wallsee Castle====
2 CONT * [http://andryuningovi.blogspot.com/2011/02/emperor-franz-josef-of-austria-on-his.html '''Wallsee Castle'''] In Wallsee, you might want to take the time to visit the 14 th -century '''Wallsee Castle''', still in the possession of
2 CONC  the Habsburgs. Past the tiny village of Ardagger, you ride under the mighty Fortress Clam. You explore the fertile farmland of the Danube Valley, with rural towns and picturesque farms. Grein with its imposing castle soon comes i
2 CONC nto view which for many is one of the highlights of the trip. With only 2,800 residents, Grein is one of Austria's smallest towns. Due to its strategic location above rapids on the Danube, the city became quite rich during the 16t
2 CONC h and 17th centuries, and the wealth is still evident in the elaborate houses built around the town square.
