0 @N6000000002188420753@ NOTE The original structure of Moncalieri Castle dates back to the 12th century. The first modification of the castle was decided by Tommaso III of Savoy in 1277. Only in the second half of the 15th century, after the marriage of Jolan
1 CONC da of Valois with Amedeo IX, the Blessed, the fortress was enlarged and provided with angular cylindrical towers and it began to take on the look of a ducal mansion. In the 16th century the castle fell into disrepair.  In the seve
1 CONC nteenth century the duke Carlo Emanuele I began the reconstruction of the castle, completed then by the Royal Lady Maria Cristina and her son Carlo Emanuele II in the following century. The works were entrusted to Carlo and Amedeo
1 CONC  di Castellamonte later. At the end of the eighteenth century Vittorio Amedeo III enlarged it furtherly by adding four square towers.  The castle was the favourite residence of the princess Maria Clotilde who died there in 1911 an
1 CONC d of Vittorio Emanuele II, the last king who chose it as his habitual residence and restored and decorated it according to the fashion of the end of the last century.  The most of the luxury furniture, gathered in different times 
1 CONC by the Savoy, has been transferred to some museums, but the magnificence of its rooms can still be admired in the Royal Chapel, in the apartments of the princesses Maria Letizia and Maria Clotilde, in the royal apartment of Vittor
1 CONC io Emanuele, in the graceful boudoir of the Queen and in the eighteenth-century reception room.  The castle belongs to the State now and Carabinieri have their barracks in a part of it.
0 @N6000000002176654986@ NOTE Umberto led his country out of its isolation and into the Triple Alliance
1 CONT with Austria and Germany. He supported the nationalistic and imperialistic
1 CONT policies that led to disaster for Italy and helped create the atmosphere in
