0 @N6000000002322320164@ NOTE Taking over the regency for his insane cousin King Otto when his father
1 CONT Luitpold died in 1912, Louis, even though King Otto was still alive at the
1 CONT time, assumed the throne of Bavaria on November 5, 1913. As new king, Louis
1 CONT III was interested chiefly in improving agriculture and transportation but he
1 CONT also continued the traditional Wittlesbach patronage of the arts. Taking as
1 CONT little part of World War I as possible, the Bavarian revolution was a
1 CONT complete surprise to Louis. Never abdicating, he died embittered in exil.
