1 CONT military organization, and left the politicians in no doubt as to his views.
1 CONT He never recovered from the death of his bride of one year. Epidemics of
1 CONT cholera and yellow fever recurred in Portugal, and he worked assiduously to
1 CONT provide relief. In October 1861, he fell ill with typhoid fever, and he and a
1 CONT younger brother died in November of 1861, succeeded by brother Louis.
