0 @N6000000002322303845@ NOTE On June 5, 1944, the day after the Allied Liberation of Rome in World War II,
1 CONT Crown Prince Umberto was named lieutenant general of the realm by his father,
1 CONT King Victor Emmanuel III, relinquishing all power for himself but retaining
1 CONT title of king. In 1946, public opinion forced a plebiscite to decide between
1 CONT the monarchy and a republican form of government. In an effort to influence
1 CONT the vote in favor of the dynasty, Victor Emmanuel abdicated in favor of his
1 CONT son on May 9, 1946, but the vote was for the republic, exiling the family.
