0 @N6000000002322315708@ NOTE Charles was the last of the Austro-Hungarian monarchy, November 21,
1 CONT 1916-November 11, 1918. A peace loving man, he made attempts to take
1 CONT Austria-Hungary out of World War I through his brother-in-law, Prince Sixtus
1 CONT von Bourbon-Parma. All failed due to the Emperor's refusal to cede any
1 CONT territories in Italy. On November 11, 1918, he renounced all participation in
1 CONT affairs of state but did not abdicate. Deposed by the Austrian parliament in
1 CONT 1919, he was exiled to Madeira, living in poor conditions dying of pnemomia.
